WEBVTT

NOTE push-failures: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.605
Read the failure count, understand
what has already been tried,

V0-2
00:00:06.705 --> 00:00:08.480
and re-push only what failed.

V1a-1
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.830
The message names how many stations
could not be updated: here, two.

V1b-1
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.898
The rest of the push succeeded.
A failure is partial,

V1b-2
00:00:21.998 --> 00:00:27.360
and the stations that verified are already
live in Lynx. The other four are done.

V2a-1
00:00:34.703 --> 00:00:38.283
Failed stations are re-pushed
automatically, up to two further attempts.

V2b-1
00:00:38.837 --> 00:00:42.820
This is the automatic retry pass,
before the failure is reported.

V2b-2
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:47.087
The bar restarts at zero and counts
only the stations being retried.

V3a-1
00:00:54.123 --> 00:00:58.282
Diagnostics reports the Lynx interconnect,
whether the cloud can be pinged,

V3a-2
00:00:58.382 --> 00:01:00.823
and the installation
and course identifiers.

V3b-1
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:04.340
If the ping is failing,
no amount of re-pushing will help.

V4a-1
00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:15.728
The stations that failed are still
pending, but they count as pushed today,

V4a-2
00:01:15.828 --> 00:01:19.957
so reopening Push Changes lists
them under Pushed Today, unticked.

V4b-1
00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:25.213
Tick them to send them again. Stations
that went through are not listed again,

V4b-2
00:01:25.313 --> 00:01:27.563
so the whole set cannot go out twice.

V4b-3
00:01:27.663 --> 00:01:31.920
Untick anything under Available to
Push that you did not mean to send.
